  "text": "Assign user roles and configure permission levels\n\nProtect sensitive clinical and financial data by tailoring access for your staff. Only practice managers and primary administrators can modify security credentials.\n\n1. Go to **Settings > Practice Staff > Roles & Permissions**.\n2. Click **Create New Role** or select an existing title from the directory.\n3. Toggle permissions across categories, including *Billing*, *Patient Charts*, and *System Settings*.\n4. Click **Assign Users**, select the staff members who require this profile, and click **Save Changes**.\n\n**Limits & Conditions:** Every active user profile must be assigned to at least one role. Direct permission overrides on individual accounts are not permitted; all restrictions must flow through the assigned role.\n\n**Troubleshooting:** If a staff member cannot view a restricted menu after saving, verify their account status is active and have them clear their browser cache before logging back in."
 },
